name: Bug report
description: Something is wrong when using this plugin via the snap
title: "[bug] "
labels: ["bug"]
body:
  - type: checkboxes
    id: native-install-check
    attributes:
      label: Before submitting
      description: >-
        "Natively" means without the snap: copying the plugin into your OBS
        Studio user configuration (~/.config/obs-studio/plugins) or using a
        distribution package. This check tells snap problems and plugin
        bugs apart, so please test it before reporting here.
      options:
        - label: I have checked that this error does not happen by installing the plugin natively
          required: true
  - type: input
    id: affected-snap
    attributes:
      label: Affected snap
      description: Name of the snap you installed
      placeholder: e.g. {{ snap_name }}
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: input
    id: versions
    attributes:
      label: Versions
      description: Snap revision and OBS Studio version
      placeholder: e.g. snap rev 12, OBS Studio 31.1
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: textarea
    id: what-happened
    attributes:
      label: What happened?
      description: Also tell us what you expected to happen instead
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: textarea
    id: steps
    attributes:
      label: Steps to reproduce
      placeholder: |
        1.
        2.
    validations:
      required: false
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        ### Is this a plugin bug?

        If the misbehavior is in the plugin itself once loaded in OBS
        Studio (wrong behavior, missing features, crashes caused by the
        plugin logic), please report it to the plugin developers upstream
        instead — check the `website` or `source-code` links on the snap
        page. This tracker is for **snap-related** problems: installation,
        connection to the OBS Studio snap, files in the wrong places, or
        anything that only happens with the snap and not with a native
        installation of the plugin.
